          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01QrDBrAW9wcHXs575n5GG9T",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022:\u0022concepts/retrieval-patterns.md\u0022,\u0022content\u0022:\u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Retrieval Patterns\\ndescription: Techniques for combining sparse lexical and dense vector search to optimize information retrieval in RAG systems.\\ntimestamp: 2026-07-14T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - concept/Retrieval\\n  - concept/Ranking\\n  - pattern/Hybrid-Search\\nconfidence: medium\\nconfidence_reason: \\u0022Single source on hybrid retrieval; core concept established but could benefit from additional corroboration.\\u0022\\n---\\n\\n## Hybrid Retrieval\\n\\n**Hybrid retrieval** combines two complementary search methods:\\n\\n- **Sparse lexical search** (e.g., BM25): matches exact terms and rare identifiers (error codes, product SKUs) with high precision.\\n- **Dense vector search**: captures semantic similarity and intent, matching paraphrases and conceptually related content.\\n\\nThese two ranked result sets are then merged, often via **reciprocal rank fusion** (RRF), which harmonizes scores from different ranking systems and produces a single consolidated ranking.\\n\\n## Why Hybrid Outperforms Single Methods\\n\\nHybrid retrieval consistently outperforms either method alone, especially on queries that mix:\\n\\n- Rare identifiers that require exact term matching (lexical strength)\\n- Natural language intent that benefits from semantic understanding (vector strength)\\n\\nThis balance has made hybrid retrieval the **default retrieval pattern in production RAG systems**.\\n\\n## Reciprocal Rank Fusion\\n\\nReciprocal rank fusion is a fusion strategy that assigns each result a normalized score based on its rank in each individual ranked list. This approach is robust to different scoring scales and is particularly effective when combining sparse and dense retrievers.\\n\\n## Citations\\n\\n[^1]: Hybrid retrieval combining sparse and dense search for RAG systems.\\n\u0022}"
        }
      ],
